Pseudo-diff F4 (seam_fp, nothing applied): read-or-recompute by price at light load.
Switch SGLANG_HICACHE_NEXT_TURN_RECOMPUTE_BY_PRICE (EnvBool False); needs the arrival gate, measured prices (PR1),
the read line (F3: measured lags) and F5's gate argument (the prompt's tokens, for the shared length).

Where the restore path is chosen at arrival. Scheduler._add_request_to_queue calls _prefetch_kvcache(req) before
the request joins the waiting queue (scheduler.py:3305-3306); that calls tree_cache.prefetch_from_storage, which
joins a staged read under the same handle (unified_radix_cache.py:2145-2149), declines below the 256-token
threshold (2189-2195) or under the rate limit (2196-2200), and then asks the arrival gate
(2201-2205, prefetch_gate_fn = NextTurnPrefetcher.prefetch_gate, next_turn_prefetch.py:1411-1446). A declined gate
leaves no entry in ongoing_prefetch, so admission takes the turn in its next pass and it prefills whatever is
missing (scheduler.py:4006-4012 skips only turns with a read under way). So "recompute instead of read" is one
more gate answer; nothing else changes, and no Scheduler line is touched.

